1
00:04:17,142 --> 00:04:23,142
It started like any other night.

2
00:08:34,285 --> 00:08:40,285
Collateral is a drama, crime, thriller film directed by Michael Mann.

3
00:12:51,428 --> 00:12:57,428
Cab driver Max picks up a man who offers him $600 to drive him around.

4
00:17:08,571 --> 00:17:14,571
But the promise of easy money sours when Max realizes his fare is an assassin.

5
00:21:25,714 --> 00:21:31,714
Vincent, played by Tom Cruise.

6
00:25:42,857 --> 00:25:48,857
Max Durocher, played by Jamie Foxx.

7
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Annie Farrell, played by Jada Pinkett Smith.

8
00:34:17,142 --> 00:34:23,142
Det. Ray Fanning, played by Mark Ruffalo.

9
00:38:34,285 --> 00:38:40,285
Richard Weidner, played by Peter Berg.

10
00:42:51,428 --> 00:42:57,428
Felix Reyes-Torrena, played by Javier Bardem.

11
00:47:08,571 --> 00:47:14,571
Collateral is a 2004 American action thriller film directed and produced by Michael
Mann, written by Stuart Beattie, and starring Tom Cruise and Jamie Foxx.

12
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
The supporting cast includes Jada Pinkett Smith, Mark Ruffalo,
Peter Berg, Javier Bardem, and Bruce McGill.

13
00:55:42,857 --> 00:55:48,857
The film follows Max Durocher (Foxx), a Los Angeles cab
driver, and his customer, Vincent (Cruise).

14
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
When offered a high fare for driving to several locations, Max agrees but soon finds himself taken
hostage by Vincent who turns out to be a sociopathic hitman on a contract killing spree.

15
01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
Beattie conceived the film's concept while taking
a taxi home from Sydney Airport.

16
01:08:34,285 --> 01:08:40,285
He shared the idea with producer Julie Richardson, who
showed it to director Frank Darabont.

17
01:12:51,428 --> 01:12:57,428
The film was pitched to HBO but was declined.

18
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
It was purchased by DreamWorks but would not see development for three years.

19
01:21:25,714 --> 01:21:31,714
Before the trio of Mann, Cruise and Foxx joined the film, Mimi Leder, Janusz Kamiński and Fernando Meirelles were each
considered as director, and Russell Crowe and Adam Sandler were in talks to star as Vincent and Max, respectively.

20
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
Filming primarily took place throughout Los Angeles, and was the first feature
film to be shot with a Viper FilmStream High-Definition Camera.

21
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The musical score was composed by James Newton Howard, with
additional songs from Audioslave and Paul Oakenfold.

22
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
Collateral was released in the United States on August 6,
2004, and grossed over $220 million worldwide.

23
01:38:34,285 --> 01:38:40,285
The film received critical acclaim in particular for the performances
of Cruise and Foxx, Mann's direction, and the editing.

24
01:42:51,428 --> 01:42:57,428
Collateral was chosen by the National Board of Review
as one of the top ten films of 2004.

25
01:47:08,571 --> 01:47:14,571
At the 77th Academy Awards, Foxx received a nomination for Best Supporting Actor, while
film editors Jim Miller and Paul Rubell were nominated for Best Film Editing.

26
01:51:25,714 --> 01:51:31,714
The film explores themes of taxi, police, hitman,
hostage, self-fulfilling prophecy.

27
01:55:42,857 --> 01:55:48,857
The tone is intense and dark and emotional.
